# A MIDI clock coming in over USB lands each pulse up to a frame (1 ms) early or late: the tempo
# followed is measured over a bar, so it holds steady (120.0 give or take 0.1; the tune's beat within about 3 ms, a pulse's
# own jitter included), and a new tempo is
# still taken within a beat or so (the last 12 pulses 4 % off the bar's)
sid @SID1@
turn K2 3
clockin 120 1
wait 300
midi fa 0 0
wait 5000
expect follow 1
expect follow_bpm >1198
expect follow_bpm <1202
wait 137
expect follow_bpm >1198
expect follow_bpm <1202
wait 211
expect follow_bpm >1198
expect follow_bpm <1202
wait 173
expect follow_bpm >1198
expect follow_bpm <1202
wait 2000
expect follow_err >-40
expect follow_err <40
clockin 140 1
wait 700
expect follow_bpm >1380
expect follow_bpm <1420
wait 3000
expect follow_bpm >1398
expect follow_bpm <1402
expect follow_err >-40
expect follow_err <40
